//! Byte-identity regression: default build (feature `boundary-rd` OFF)
//! must produce bit-for-bit identical output to pre-boundary-RD
//! `origin/main`.
//!
//! This test is the **only reason** the boundary-RD feature exists as
//! an opt-in Cargo flag: users who don't opt in MUST NOT see any
//! behavioral drift from the refinement plumbing.
//!
//! Hashes were generated by extracting `origin/main` (commit
//! `aae28ce8118fafbd6eb38ac1150cb6d5fe6edbee`) into a clean build tree,
//! dropping the lineart corpus into the same relative path, and running
//! the same encode config against each PNG. The hashes in this file
//! match both origin/main and the current worktree's default build.
//!
//! # When a hash here drifts
//!
//! - **Expected failure:** you intentionally changed encoder behavior
//!   and bumped the `values_archmage.csv` hash in `locked_values.rs`.
//!   Regenerate these hashes alongside those.
//!
//! - **Unexpected failure:** the boundary-RD gating leaked into the
//!   default path. Stop, diff against origin/main, find the leak.
//!
//! This test intentionally runs **regardless of feature flags** so that
//! a user who accidentally enables `boundary-rd` via a dep still gets
//! byte-identity protection for the `BoundaryRd::Off` default.

